      "say": "React updates the screen in three steps. A trigger, like a state change. Then render, where React calls your components to work out what the UI should be. And finally commit, where it applies only the minimal changes to the DOM.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-04-rendering/phases.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "triggers",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 10.0,
      "text": "What causes a re-render?",
      "visual": "chips",
      "items": [
        [
          "Its own state changed",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "Its parent re-rendered",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "A context it reads changed",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "Not: a plain variable changing",
          "red"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "A component re-renders when its own state changes, when its parent re-renders, or when a context it reads changes. Changing a plain variable does nothing.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-04-rendering/triggers.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "pure",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 13.0,
      "text": "Rendering must be pure.",
      "visual": "chips",
      "items": [
        [
          "Same inputs, same output",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "No mutating outside variables",
          "red"
        ],
        [
          "No fetching while rendering",
          "red"
        ],
        [
          "StrictMode double-renders to catch it",
          "yellow"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "Rendering has to be pure: the same props and state always produce the same output. Don't mutate outside variables or fetch data while rendering. Strict Mode renders twice in development to help you catch it.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-04-rendering/pure.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "cascade",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 14.0,
      "text": "Children re-render with their parent.",
      "visual": "flow",
      "badge": "RENDERING IS CHEAP, THE DOM IS NOT",
      "items": [
        [
          "App",
          "yellow",
          "state changes here"
        ],
        [
          "Sidebar",
          "blue",
          "re-renders too"
        ],
        [
          "Post",
          "blue",
          "re-renders too"
        ],
        [
          "Real DOM",
          "green",
          "only changed bits"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "When a component re-renders, all of its children re-render too, even if their props didn't change. That is normally fine, because rendering is cheap, and React only touches the real DOM where something actually changed.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-04-rendering/cascade.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "batch",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 8.5,
      "text": "Updates are batched.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "function onClick() {",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  setA(1);",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  setB(2);",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  setC(3);",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "}",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "// ONE render, not three",
          "pink"
